From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:02:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Save sync: never replace a cloud save that was not compared,
 and let the player choose when both changed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three ways the cloud's save could be lost:

- When the cloud's save did not arrive within FETCH_MS (an iCloud download that takes longer than 10 s), the game played on with this device's save, and the sender then moved the cloud's save into a local backup and replaced it with this device's at the next Commit.
- On the first play on a device, with no save there and a slow download, the game's first save replaced the cloud's progress the same way.
- When both sides had changed since the last sync, the newer save time won without asking.

send_save now replaces only what it compared against: no save, the save last synced (<save>.sync), or a damaged file, which is kept in the backups first. A cloud save that changed since this device's last sync, or one a device that never synced finds, is not replaced: the save is not sent, and the log says so once.

ss_decide returns SS_ASK when both changed (or a device's first sync finds a save on both sides) instead of comparing times. The mount then plays on with this device's save and sends nothing.

A front end that compared the two saves before the start passes the player's choice in DM_SAVE_SYNC_CHOICE: cloud:<hash> brings in the cloud's save with that hash, local:<hash> (or local:none) lets this device's replace it, keeping the cloud's in <save>-backups/<date> cloud, and offline skips the wait for a cloud that could not be read. A choice holds only for the cloud save it names. Mac apps say they read it with DMSaveSyncChoice=1 in Info.plist.

t_save_sync covers: both changed with no choice, a choice of either side, a choice made on an older cloud save, the cloud unreadable at the start and readable at the next Commit, the Mac launcher's send after the host, an offline start, the first play on a new device and a damaged cloud file.

Front-ends: new: DM_SAVE_SYNC_CHOICE (cloud:<hash>, local:<hash>, local:none, offline) carries the player's choice when the cloud's save and this device's both changed; Mac apps advertise it with DMSaveSyncChoice=1 in Info.plist
Front-ends: interface: a save that changed on both sides is no longer replaced by the newer one; it stays on both sides until a front end passes the player's choice (the log says "both changed: …")

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1785
Reason: A cloud save that was not compared is never replaced, and the player chooses when both sides changed (#957)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#957

